SHELL/BASH Scripting:
`````````````````````
To execute multiple objects [cmds] using single object [file].

extension: .bash or .sh

To run:
```````
# bash script.sh
OR
# ./script.sh [to execute the script: chmod u+x file.sh]










First line of script must be: [shebang]

#! : shebang
env: /bin/bash, /bin/sh









++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
# vim script.sh

#!/bin/bash
cmd1
cmd2
cmd3

# bash script.sh
...
